  "summary": "Extends the `checktxinputs_invalid_transactions_test` helper in `transaction_tests.cpp` to support transactions with multiple inputs. Adds a test case where two inputs are individually valid under `MoneyRange` but their sum exceeds `MAX_MONEY`. This verifies that `Consensus::CheckTxInputs` rejects transactions whose cumulative input values exceed consensus limits.",
  "problem": "Existing unit tests for `Consensus::CheckTxInputs` only tested single-input transactions where `coin.out.nValue == nValueIn`. Consequently, mutations or bugs in the cumulative value check `!MoneyRange(nValueIn)` (such as switching `||` to `&&` in the out-of-range condition) passed unit tests undetected.",
